WEBVTT

﻿1

00:11:23.708 --> 00:11:28.915
Big brother, is that the way
to America over there?


00:11:29.125 --> 00:11:31.957
No, this is the way.


00:11:32.166 --> 00:11:34.790
This way?


00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:38.249
They say that if you dig a hole-


00:11:38.458 --> 00:11:42.499
-you'll come out on
the other side ofthe world.


00:11:44.208 --> 00:11:47.999
America is on the
other side ofthe world.


00:11:48.208 --> 00:11:53.499
-But you can't just do that.
-Why not? You just said you could.


00:11:53.708 --> 00:11:58.957
Because inside the earth,
there's a fire.


00:11:59.166 --> 00:12:03.707
-Is it a big fire?
-Yes, big and hot.


00:12:05.375 --> 00:12:07.707
Really?


00:12:29.291 --> 00:12:35.624
Big brother...


00:12:35.833 --> 00:12:38.415
I was sleeping.


00:12:44.958 --> 00:12:50.874
I just wanted to make sure
you were still there.


00:12:51.083 --> 00:12:58.249
Of course I am. Where did you
think I was going? Go back to sleep.


00:13:00.625 --> 00:13:02.665
Big brother...


00:13:05.541 --> 00:13:09.124
When is mother coming home?


00:13:11.708 --> 00:13:17.749
Do you think she'll be home
for my birthday?


00:13:17.958 --> 00:13:20.415
Go back to sleep.


00:19:05.500 --> 00:19:07.915
-Mother!
-Badong?


00:19:08.125 --> 00:19:12.582
I'm so happy to hear your voice!
How are you?


00:19:12.791 --> 00:19:16.624
Mother, I have something
important to tell you.


00:19:16.833 --> 00:19:21.415
Manuel misses you.


00:19:21.625 --> 00:19:26.332
I miss him too.
I think of you both all the time.


00:19:26.541 --> 00:19:31.957
I'm OK, but Manuel is so young.


00:19:32.166 --> 00:19:35.332
He wants you to
come home for his birthday.


00:19:35.541 --> 00:19:38.749
I want that too, my son.


00:19:38.958 --> 00:19:41.624
Don't worry.


00:19:41.833 --> 00:19:47.415
I bought lots of toys
and put them in a box.


00:19:47.625 --> 00:19:53.457
-What do you think he might like?
-He likes basketball.


00:19:53.666 --> 00:19:58.582
Is that so?
I'll buy him a basketball.


00:19:58.791 --> 00:20:01.915
But when are you coming home
for real?


00:20:02.125 --> 00:20:06.915
My brother misses you so much.


00:20:18.083 --> 00:20:20.499
Do you know
what you can do for him?


00:20:20.708 --> 00:20:23.874
Take your brother to visit
our new home.


00:20:24.083 --> 00:20:28.999
You can show him what
it will look like when I come back.


00:20:29.208 --> 00:20:34.540
Show him where his room will be,
and yours and mine too.


00:20:34.750 --> 00:20:40.165
If you do that, my boy-


00:20:40.375 --> 00:20:43.832
-you'll make your brother happy.


00:20:44.041 --> 00:20:47.332
That would make me happy too.


00:20:47.541 --> 00:20:53.540
I'm coming home soon
and we'll all live together.


00:20:55.958 --> 00:20:58.665
I love you so much.


00:20:58.875 --> 00:21:05.124
You're very good
and I'm so proud of you.


00:22:44.250 --> 00:22:47.207
Good morning.


00:22:53.083 --> 00:22:57.999
This is the living room. The sofa
will be there and the TV here.


00:23:00.000 --> 00:23:02.415
Will the floor look like this?


00:23:02.625 --> 00:23:06.874
They'll put a carpet on it.
That will make it nicer, right?


00:23:07.083 --> 00:23:10.207
Why are there no windows?


00:23:10.416 --> 00:23:15.582
It's not finished.
Uncle will put windows in.


00:23:15.791 --> 00:23:19.540
Why is this so rough?
Are they going to paint it?


00:23:19.750 --> 00:23:25.915
When our house is done,
it'll be as nice as that one.


00:23:26.125 --> 00:23:29.457
But why isn't there a roof?


00:23:29.666 --> 00:23:34.165
They'll put one on.
It's not finished yet.


00:23:34.375 --> 00:23:38.915
-Uncle, when will the house be done?
-I don't know.


00:23:39.125 --> 00:23:41.707
Mother said I should tell you
to hurry up.


00:23:41.916 --> 00:23:45.165
-Your mother said that?
-Yes.


00:23:45.375 --> 00:23:49.040
Well then, tell your mother
to send more money.


00:23:49.250 --> 00:23:52.082
The roof could have been
finished this week-


00:23:52.291 --> 00:23:57.082
-but I couldn't pay the workers.
You tell her that.


00:43:46.250 --> 00:43:50.124
In the name ofthe Father,
the Son and the Holy Ghost. Amen.


00:43:50.333 --> 00:43:53.915
May the Lord be with you.


00:43:54.125 --> 00:44:00.499
May the sacrifice we have offered
renew our spirit.


00:44:00.708 --> 00:44:02.749
For the sake of your Son...


00:44:17.041 --> 00:44:21.665
May the peace of the Lord
be with you always.


00:44:21.875 --> 00:44:25.374
Let us offer each other
the sign of peace.


00:44:32.916 --> 00:44:35.874
My name is Jackie.


00:44:48.458 --> 00:44:51.790
Nanny Gloria.


00:55:24.041 --> 00:55:27.624
Ears...


00:55:27.833 --> 00:55:34.165
Nose...


00:55:34.375 --> 00:55:38.332
Eyebrows...


00:55:41.125 --> 00:55:44.124
Eyes...


00:55:51.583 --> 00:55:54.999
Hand...


00:55:55.208 --> 00:56:00.749
-Blanket...
-Yes, blanket.


00:56:00.958 --> 00:56:07.874
Blouse...


00:56:08.083 --> 00:56:12.707
-Foot...
-Foot, yes.


00:56:14.166 --> 00:56:18.207
Calf...


00:58:30.583 --> 00:58:35.124
I wonderwhat mother
is doing in America right now.


00:58:35.333 --> 00:58:40.290
-I don't know. Maybe she's sleeping.
-Sleeping? But it's noon already!


00:58:40.500 --> 00:58:43.874
-It's nighttime in America.
-Nighttime?


00:58:44.083 --> 00:58:48.415
If it's daytime in the Philippines,
it's nighttime in America.


00:58:48.625 --> 00:58:50.749
I didn't know that.


00:58:53.375 --> 00:58:56.540
How long will she be staying there?


00:58:56.750 --> 00:59:01.707
Why are you asking
all these questions?


00:59:01.916 --> 00:59:05.249
I'm just thinking of her.


00:59:05.458 --> 00:59:08.915
We'll be all grown up
by the time she gets back.


00:59:09.125 --> 00:59:11.832
What? But I'm still a little boy.


00:59:12.041 --> 00:59:18.707
She'll come home when we're done
with school and have jobs.


00:59:56.083 --> 00:59:58.915
It's Salvador.
I want you to come home!


00:59:59.125 --> 01:00:04.457
What's happened?
Is there a problem?


01:00:04.666 --> 01:00:07.374
No, you just need to come home.


01:00:07.583 --> 01:00:13.457
I know you need to earn money
for the new house and everything-


01:00:13.666 --> 01:00:16.749
-but I'm bigger now.
I can help you.


01:00:16.958 --> 01:00:21.499
I'll work and make money
so that you can come home.


01:00:21.708 --> 01:00:27.749
No. I'm the one that's going to work
for you and your brother.


01:00:30.541 --> 01:00:33.665
I love you so much.


01:00:35.833 --> 01:00:40.915
You must be strong.
Stop crying, alright?


01:00:41.125 --> 01:00:46.665
-You have to come home.
-Please don't cry.


01:00:46.875 --> 01:00:49.207
You have to be strong.


01:00:50.750 --> 01:00:57.415
-Come home!
-I love you and Manuel so much.


01:01:04.125 --> 01:01:08.290
-Do you need help?
-No, ask him.


01:01:08.500 --> 01:01:14.624
You're too young
and fishing is hard work.


01:01:14.833 --> 01:01:19.665
I can help with the fishing nets.


01:01:19.875 --> 01:01:25.082
No, we can take care of it.
Perhaps when you're older...


01:01:33.250 --> 01:01:39.165
Good day. I was wondering,
could I work here?


01:01:39.375 --> 01:01:43.165
That's not possible.
You're too young.


01:01:43.375 --> 01:01:47.040
I'm good at cooking,
I always help my grandma at home.


01:01:47.250 --> 01:01:54.124
-It's not possible... Go away.
-I'm a fast learner.


01:01:54.333 --> 01:01:58.332
-Good afternoon.
-Good afternoon to you.


01:01:58.541 --> 01:02:02.207
I'm just wondering
if there's work for me here.


01:02:05.625 --> 01:02:10.040
See this sack of rice...
It must be emptied.


01:02:10.250 --> 01:02:15.290
Put this plastic bag on the scale.
You're going to repack the rice.


01:02:15.500 --> 01:02:18.540
Each plastic bag should weigh 1 kilo.


01:02:18.750 --> 01:02:24.290
Put the rice in the plastic bag,
like this.


01:02:24.500 --> 01:02:29.874
Just make sure the scale needle
doesn't go past number one.


01:02:30.083 --> 01:02:34.707
It doesn't matter if it goes
under the line, but not over.


01:02:34.916 --> 01:02:37.582
Mother, I can't do this any longer.


01:02:37.791 --> 01:02:42.915
Gloria, I know you can do it.
You're strong.


01:02:43.125 --> 01:02:45.249
I feel like my chest will explode.


01:02:45.458 --> 01:02:51.415
Mother, I'll never get used
to this. Not ever!


01:02:51.625 --> 01:02:54.874
This is not what God wants.


01:02:55.083 --> 01:02:59.582
You feel that way now.
but I believe it's God's will-


01:02:59.791 --> 01:03:02.499
-that you give your children
a betterfuture.


01:03:02.708 --> 01:03:04.874
No, mother!


01:03:05.083 --> 01:03:10.832
God wants me to be with my children.


01:03:11.041 --> 01:03:13.999
Can you understand that?


01:03:14.208 --> 01:03:16.540
-I want to come home.
-No...


01:03:16.750 --> 01:03:19.207
I miss my children.


01:03:19.416 --> 01:03:23.540
Be strong my child,
you can do it.


01:03:23.750 --> 01:03:30.832
Try to be strong.
I know you can do it.


01:03:34.791 --> 01:03:37.374
I'm done now.


01:03:39.208 --> 01:03:42.624
-Are you finished?
-Yes.


01:03:42.833 --> 01:03:47.457
-Is the sack empty?
-Yes.


01:03:47.666 --> 01:03:51.832
Let me see.
You're a really good boy.


01:03:52.041 --> 01:03:57.082
Wait, l'll go inside.
I have a reward for you.


01:04:04.875 --> 01:04:08.832
Here you are...
Some candy and mangojuice.


01:04:09.041 --> 01:04:12.540
-That's your favourite, isn't it?
-Yes, thank you.


01:04:12.750 --> 01:04:17.624
You're a really nice boy,
a hard working boy.


01:04:19.750 --> 01:04:21.915
You like that, don't you?


01:04:30.333 --> 01:04:35.207
I just wanted to ask how...


01:04:35.416 --> 01:04:38.290
What?


01:04:38.500 --> 01:04:45.457
-How much will you pay me?
-Pay you?


01:04:45.666 --> 01:04:50.207
-I'm not giving you any money.
-But you must pay me.


01:04:50.416 --> 01:04:54.540
-I did all of this.
- Did you help me for money?


01:04:54.750 --> 01:04:59.207
Get out of here. Shame on you!
Are you trying to trick me?


01:04:59.416 --> 01:05:05.790
Go on, leave! Shame on you!
I'm not that easily fooled!


01:13:10.541 --> 01:13:14.040
-And no sex?
-No.


01:13:15.458 --> 01:13:18.874
-Nothing?
-No.


01:13:19.083 --> 01:13:21.499
-Where is he from?
-America.


01:13:21.708 --> 01:13:23.749
I love Americans.


01:13:23.958 --> 01:13:26.915
I hate them,
but this one was different.


01:13:27.125 --> 01:13:31.832
-You hate Americans?
-Why?


01:13:32.041 --> 01:13:34.540
They think they're so good in bed.


01:13:34.750 --> 01:13:38.832
The Italians are worse.


01:13:39.041 --> 01:13:43.082
Yes, they think they're so good,
they shouldn't have to pay.


01:13:43.291 --> 01:13:49.624
-But the Germans are the worst.
-The Germans? They're OK.


01:13:49.833 --> 01:13:53.582
They're dirty.


01:13:53.791 --> 01:13:56.165
No, not all ofthem.


01:13:56.375 --> 01:14:02.999
But the Arabs...
The Arabs are the worst of all.


01:14:03.208 --> 01:14:08.832
-I wouldn't go with them.
-Nobody would. They stink.


01:14:09.041 --> 01:14:14.124
How about the Japanese?
I wouldn't go with them.


01:14:14.333 --> 01:14:17.749
No way, not with a Jap...
I hate the Japanese.


01:14:17.958 --> 01:14:22.790
You wouldn't because their dicks
are the size of my little finger.


01:14:23.000 --> 01:14:27.707
My little finger, not yours.


01:14:27.916 --> 01:14:32.874
I'm going to look for him tomorrow.
I know where he lives.


01:17:34.291 --> 01:17:39.165
Time to get up!
We're going somewhere today.


01:17:39.375 --> 01:17:43.457
Hurry up and get dressed.
Wake up!


01:17:43.666 --> 01:17:47.457
-But I have school today.
-You're not going to school.


01:17:49.208 --> 01:17:51.290
I'll be your teacher today.


01:17:56.750 --> 01:18:01.332
This is yours...
...and this is yours.


01:18:03.625 --> 01:18:08.040
Tell your brother's teacher
he's home sick today.


01:18:12.583 --> 01:18:15.707
So you've worked
for that old miserly cheat!


01:18:15.916 --> 01:18:18.790
Rita told me everything.


01:18:19.000 --> 01:18:24.165
-I take good care ofyou, don't I?
-Yes, grandmother.


01:18:24.375 --> 01:18:30.499
So why do you keep calling
your mother to complain?


01:18:41.500 --> 01:18:43.874
Do you know where we're going?


01:18:52.291 --> 01:18:54.332
Let's go.


01:19:19.791 --> 01:19:21.999
Look at them.


01:19:25.041 --> 01:19:28.207
This is what they do every day.


01:19:34.208 --> 01:19:39.374
Look at those kids.
Is this the kind of life you want?


01:19:43.416 --> 01:19:49.624
Look, he's only your age
and he's already collecting garbage.


01:20:10.791 --> 01:20:14.457
-Here's some bread, eat it!
-I don't want it.


01:20:14.666 --> 01:20:18.457
Why not?
You haven't eaten anything today.


01:20:18.666 --> 01:20:21.249
Go on, eat it!


01:20:21.458 --> 01:20:25.374
Do you know why your mother
is working in America?


01:20:25.583 --> 01:20:29.374
So you won't have to eat this bread.


01:20:29.583 --> 01:20:33.332
So that you can have a good life.


01:20:33.541 --> 01:20:38.624
A good life, proper food, nice house.


01:20:38.833 --> 01:20:41.999
A good education.


01:20:42.208 --> 01:20:46.040
Money, so when you get sick
you can go to the doctor.


01:20:46.250 --> 01:20:50.082
Those kids can't go to the doctor.


01:20:52.958 --> 01:20:58.582
When they get sick, they just die.


01:20:58.791 --> 01:21:01.290
Theyjust die.


01:21:14.291 --> 01:21:16.665
Are you enjoying your ice cream?


01:21:23.208 --> 01:21:26.749
We should pity those people
who live in the dumpsite.


01:21:26.958 --> 01:21:31.290
No one should have to live
in a place like that.


01:21:33.250 --> 01:21:40.707
You know, there's something worse
happening here at night.


01:21:42.083 --> 01:21:45.499
Kids come here to sell themselves.


01:21:45.708 --> 01:21:50.832
-Sell themselves?
-They sell themselves to tourists.


01:21:51.041 --> 01:21:54.582
They buy kids and take
them to their hotels.


01:21:54.791 --> 01:21:58.707
Why are they taking the kids
to their hotels?


01:21:58.916 --> 01:22:03.290
I don't know, they just want
someone to sleep with.


01:22:04.583 --> 01:22:07.457
Do they get paid?


01:22:07.666 --> 01:22:11.832
What else do they do?


01:22:12.041 --> 01:22:18.624
Let's not talk about it.
They just sleep, nothing else.


01:22:18.833 --> 01:22:24.082
They don't do anything,
they just sleep there.


01:22:24.291 --> 01:22:26.665
Just eat your ice cream.


01:39:15.500 --> 01:39:19.290
Hey, that's my bike.
What are you doing with it?


01:39:19.500 --> 01:39:25.832
-It's mine now.
-It's not yours, it's ours.


01:39:26.041 --> 01:39:28.790
Your slippers... take them off.


01:39:29.000 --> 01:39:32.582
-Take off your clothes.
-Do you have any money?


01:39:33.916 --> 01:39:37.332
You're new around here,
don't be a show off!


01:39:43.458 --> 01:39:47.207
Hey, go away!


01:40:54.208 --> 01:40:56.665
Wake up!


01:40:56.875 --> 01:40:59.165
It's time to eat soon.


01:41:01.208 --> 01:41:08.040
-Have you seen your brother?
-No.


01:41:19.666 --> 01:41:24.124
-Have you seen Salvador?
-No.


01:41:24.333 --> 01:41:29.415
It's very early and he's not here.
I wonder where he is.


01:41:29.625 --> 01:41:33.374
He's probably just hanging
out with the neighbours.


01:41:33.583 --> 01:41:37.499
-Are you sure you haven't seen him?
-Yes.


01:44:14.500 --> 01:44:17.290
-Have you seen Badong?
-No, I haven't.


01:44:17.500 --> 01:44:21.707
He's not in his room
and his bike is missing.


01:44:21.916 --> 01:44:24.874
Big brother!


01:44:27.541 --> 01:44:31.582
-Miss, have you seen Badong?
-No, I haven't.


01:44:31.791 --> 01:44:35.165
OK. Thank you.


01:45:04.625 --> 01:45:11.415
There's a child here!
He's bleeding. Help me!


01:45:12.958 --> 01:45:16.165
Check his pulse.


01:45:16.375 --> 01:45:19.249
Call an ambulance.
Hurry up!


01:45:19.458 --> 01:45:22.457
Where is he?


01:45:22.666 --> 01:45:26.874
He's still breathing.
Help me carry him.


01:46:02.166 --> 01:46:05.082
We need a tricycle!


01:46:31.791 --> 01:46:36.415
Hello...
Gloria, is that you?


01:46:40.500 --> 01:46:44.874
My dear daughter,
I don't know how to say this...


01:46:45.083 --> 01:46:48.707
...but something's happened
to Salvador.


01:52:23.250 --> 01:52:28.165
-This is a very nice pen.
-I'm not really interested in pens.


01:52:28.375 --> 01:52:33.290
I'll give you 25 dollars for all
of these, you'll get less elsewhere.


01:52:33.500 --> 01:52:38.082
-Only 25 dollars?
-25, max.


01:52:38.291 --> 01:52:41.665
I can't give you more.
This one's a copy.


01:52:41.875 --> 01:52:47.165
Okay, I'll give you 30.
That's my last offer. Agreed?


01:55:04.666 --> 01:55:07.790
I'm here now, my son.


01:55:09.375 --> 01:55:12.374
I will never leave you again.


01:55:30.666 --> 01:55:34.624
Never ever.


01:55:36.208 --> 01:55:40.915
How are you, my sweet one?
Are you not asleep yet?


01:55:43.333 --> 01:55:49.165
I miss you. Do you miss me?


01:55:49.375 --> 01:55:54.915
I'll be coming to see you soon.


01:55:55.125 --> 01:55:58.249
I promise to come and see you.


01:56:00.250 --> 01:56:04.790
Are you falling asleep?
Do you want me to sing you a lullaby?


01:56:06.500 --> 01:56:11.415
Close your eyes


01:56:11.625 --> 01:56:15.499
And have a sweet dream,
my dear child


01:56:15.708 --> 01:56:23.374
I'll be here to protect you
and to watch over you

